{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Upon them</b> — on account of the springs." "<b>Dwell</b> — every bird, for the place is dry ground; no living thing is in it." "<b>Branches</b> — some say: from עֵפָה. But the correct in my eyes: like עָלִים, and עֲפָאִים is fine." "<b>Give voice</b> — like: melody."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:12.310588946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}